Under the setting where only the Value matrix $W^V$ is optimized, the loss function $f(W^V)$ satisfies:\begin{enumerate} \item \textbf{Convexity:} $f$ is convex with respect to $W^V$. 

\item \textbf{Smoothness:} $\nabla _{W^V} f$ is $L$-Lipschitz continuous for some finite constant $L > 0$. 

\item \textbf{Global Convergence:} For a learning rate $\eta \le 1/L$, gradient descent converges sublinearly: 

\begin{equation}  f(W^V_t) - f(W^{V*}) \le \frac{\| W^V_0 - W^{V*}\| _F^2}{2\eta t} = \mathcal{O}(1/t), \end{equation}

 where $W^{V*}$ is an optimal solution with $f(W^{V*}) = 0$. 

\end{enumerate}

